id: pm-github-3it2
title: Make scheduled closeout and sync refusals actionable
description: "Scheduled fleet closeout fails behind a generic workflow refusal; sync also fails import or repeat-idempotency gates. Diagnose real scheduled jobs in at least four repositories and repair package-owned causes without editing callers. Related historical closeout policy work: pm-github-f1ev and pm-github-2o9k."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: closeout,diagnostics,github-actions,sync
created_at: "2026-10-27T03:21:33.321Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T09:45:59.719Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Record exact run/job evidence across four repositories for both workflows; compare current published release with caller pins. Scheduled closeout and sync either succeed or emit one precise safe actionable diagnostic identifying the failed API read or tracker item and validation requirement. Cover each failure class with real tracker and HTTP/workflow regression tests, record behavioral revert proof, pass unchanged npm and Bun release gates, and open an unmerged PR with green CI."
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T03:22:31.152Z",codex-agent,"Orientation found historical policy and strict-close-field items, but neither covers the observed scheduled import timestamp churn or discarded command failures. Tracking this incident here. Read job logs for pm-beads 121491897462/121456680882, pm-brief 121491496493/121484867381, pm-changelog 121492220507/121514139043, and pm-vcs 121491561782/121426304352. Sync timestamp-only second-import diffs and the pm-changelog absolute-host-path pre-write gate refusal are confirmed. Closeout stderr is discarded by the workflow, requiring read-only replay before attributing the refusal. Published pm-github 2026.10.26 still contains both the administration-only required_status_checks read and generic workflow refusal."
  "2026-10-27T03:31:14.601Z",codex-agent,"Exact closeout replay: pm-github 2026.10.19 against copied tracker snapshots from all four scheduled run heads fails on GET /repos/unbraind/{repo}/pulls pagination with Unverifiable GitHub pagination. Live pm-beads Link uses /repositories/1234855396/pulls?page=2 whereas the guard requires the original /repos/unbraind/pm-beads/pulls pathname. The current 2026.10.26 release retains that guard. The fix verifies /repos/{owner}/{repo} id and full_name before following same-origin numeric aliases for the identical endpoint suffix; cycles, foreign repositories and endpoint changes remain refused. API errors now retain a safe endpoint/status diagnostic; administration-only protection 403/404 remains fail-closed unless required contexts are explicitly declared. Sync job 121514139043 refuses github-issue-226 and github-issue-1 body fields under absolute-host-path; this is a legitimate source-content gate refusal and must not be bypassed."
  "2026-10-27T03:37:29.720Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only pages() with origin/main, retaining the new tests and other functions. node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"scheduled numeric pagination none\" test/scheduled-refusals.test.ts failed 1/1 with Unverifiable GitHub pagination; restored pages() afterward. Fixed real-workflow/API acceptance passed 3/3: scheduled closeout follows verified numeric pagination with declared checks and publishes delivery; permission-limited read token produces exactly one endpoint/status error and leaves the branch unpublished; identical repeated source import preserves item and history bytes. Command: npm run build && npm run build:test && node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"scheduled repeat|scheduled closeout|permission-limited read token\" test/scheduled-refusals.test.ts test/closeout-workflow.test.ts. Current 2026.10.26 SDK lifecycle finalization fixes the old sync native-clock churn, so no new lifecycle rewrite is needed. A bounded real pm-beads replay also follows its numeric page after verifying repository identity, then stops before PR evaluation; no tracker writes."
  "2026-10-27T03:40:03.007Z",codex-agent,"Additional behavioral revert proofs: restoring only closeoutFailureReason() to origin/main makes the new diagnostic regression fail 1/1 because required policy fields disappear; restoring only the changed HTTP request error stanza makes the non-retryable 404 regression fail 1/1 because GET /repos/a/b disappears. Both implementations were restored after their proofs. The focused incident suite passed 13/13 with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Open follow-up pm-github-samq records caller-owned pin adoption, required-checks alignment and pm-changelog source-content remediation; no callers are modified here."
  "2026-10-27T03:42:50.318Z",codex-agent,"The linked pm test runner passed the incident suite 13/13; two additional pagination rejection cases now cover named foreign links and prefixed-base mismatches. Real workflow refusal reporter acceptance passed 1/1 across four receipt cases (close validation, privacy finding, synthetic credential redaction, timestamp drift), always one annotation and no remote branch. Full npm and Bun release gates will run sequentially under isolated CI Git identity with node test concurrency capped at two; coverage thresholds and source inventory are unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T03:48:01.178Z",codex-agent,"The final linked incident run passed 15/15, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Initial npm release gate passed static and full-object privacy checks, then was deliberately stopped at coverage startup while updating legacy sync workflow assertions to expect the new single stdout annotation instead of discarded stderr. That interrupted run is not a gate pass. The sync adversarial and opt-in workflow cases are being checked before restarting the unchanged full gate."
  "2026-10-27T04:01:10.298Z",codex-agent,"Correction and stronger reproduction: the earlier one-new-issue repeat case was insufficient. A mixed batch with one new issue and one pre-existing provenance-linked native item reproduces timestamp-only churn on BOTH 2026.10.19 and current 2026.10.26. The old run selects native create history as context initially, then selects an unmarked SDK update event as external context on repeat; that changes the transaction identity and updates all entries again despite identical source projection. The new runImport guard recognizes a complete unchanged projection, including body/type/description and optional assignment fields, and avoids an unnecessary item transaction only when no GitHub SDK journal is unfinished. Real mixed-batch byte-identity, local body-drift repair and unfinished-journal guard acceptance passed 2/2. The existing SDK lifecycle adapter alone does not fix this incident."
  "2026-10-27T04:02:53.736Z",codex-agent,"The exact mixed-batch context trace is now confirmed: first selected context for issue #2 is the native create event; repeat selects its intermediate update event with no message marker. The batch receives a fresh journal and changes only native clocks for already-matching entries. Both 2026.10.19 and 2026.10.26 reproduce it. Behavioral runImport-only revert fails the new mixed-batch regression (1/1); the fixed path passes real byte identity, local content repair and pending-journal cases. No-op applies report unchanged=true and do not invent a committed transaction ID. Existing completed-journal receipt assertions now reflect that behavior; actual interrupted-journal recovery assertions remain intact."
  "2026-10-27T04:05:38.832Z",codex-agent,"Final runImport-only behavioral revert now fails specifically on mixed-batch item/history byte identity (1/1), then the fixed function was restored. The focused actual interrupted-import recovery test plus mixed repeat/local drift/pending journal and comparison cases passed 3/3. Sync adversarial and explicit opt-in workflow cases passed 4/4, including every malicious fixture, a single safe annotation, no credential output, and no remote publication. Lint and zero-duplication checks pass with the final no-op implementation. Restarting linked incident verification and full npm release acceptance; an unchanged receipt has no transaction ID because no SDK transaction ran."
  "2026-10-27T04:18:13.201Z",codex-agent,"Added a real workflow test for an SDK close policy refusal, beyond the receipt-format unit case. Failed JSON closeout now writes its complete report to private stdout before the host formats/budgets the error, and the reporter prefers that complete failed report over stderr. This preserves exact item/PR/field diagnostics even if the host error envelope is abbreviated. The in-flight npm coverage attempt was stopped for this source change and is not a pass; full gates will restart after focused verification."
  "2026-10-27T04:19:18.878Z",codex-agent,"Real SDK policy-refusal workflow and full-receipt precedence acceptance passed 2/2, zero failures/skips/cancellations. The actual workflow retained failed=1 in its private JSON report and emitted exactly one annotation naming the item, PR and required reviewer field, without private policy prose or a remote branch. Restarting full npm acceptance on the final implementation; earlier interrupted attempts are not gate evidence."
  "2026-10-27T04:31:35.733Z",codex-agent,"Final parser/CLI-mode acceptance passed 4/4: SDK partial-close errors in both JSON and text modes, malformed PR JSON holding active items without raw prose, and malformed policy/non-Error pagination failures. Added these explicit branches before restarting strict all-source coverage; the runtime implementation is unchanged. The interrupted npm attempt is not a gate pass. Running the complete linked incident suite, then npm release:check and Bun sequentially at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-27T06:22:56.163Z",codex-agent,"Full npm test execution completed: 1540 tests, 1538 passed, 2 failed, zero skipped/cancelled. Both failures are existing test/import-regex.test.ts timing guards: 20000-space privacy scan measured 94.556 ms and 3000-prefix privacy scan measured 104.731 ms against unchanged 50 ms limits. All functional incident and existing behavior tests passed. Coverage aggregation is still running. The scanner currently builds two quote-state maps even for inputs without absolute-path candidates; investigating that redundant work without altering detection rules or timing thresholds."
  "2026-10-27T06:31:15.328Z",codex-agent,"The failed full npm run produced exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 22 authored modules, but is not a gate pass because two existing 50 ms scanner checks failed. Isolated c8 rerun passed 8/8 and measured 20.002 ms and 12.723 ms, confirming sensitivity to shared-host load. A small scanner optimization now computes quote-state maps only for absolute-host-path candidates and shares the map when decoding changes nothing; detection rules, offsets and timing budgets are unchanged. Existing raw/serialized/escaped/fenced path cases validate the behavior. Full gates will restart sequentially after focused acceptance."
  "2026-10-27T06:32:17.763Z",codex-agent,"The optimized scanner passed all 26 focused existing privacy/parity tests under c8. Best-of-three timings: 20000-space trigger 4.331 ms and 3000-prefix trigger 4.598 ms, with both original 50 ms limits unchanged. The complete npm release gate is running again after changelog generation/check. GitHub still reports main at 2b71f73 and latest release v2026.10.26, so neither incident cause is fixed by an intervening release."
  "2026-10-27T08:27:11.218Z",codex-agent,"Complete npm run release:check passed under isolated CI Git identity: 1540/1540 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; exact coverage across all 22 authored modules: lines/statements 12463/12463, functions 381/381, branches 4604/4604. Typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, zero duplication, full-object privacy, production audit, package dry-run, changelog and publish-attestation checks passed. The original scanner timing limits passed at 4.492 ms and 3.002 ms in this full run. Starting bun run release:check sequentially with the same unchanged gates."
  "2026-10-27T09:42:19.607Z",codex-agent,"Resume checkpoint and exact incident causes: historical closeout logs discarded command stderr; read-only 2026.10.19 replays against the four recorded run heads identify Unverifiable GitHub pagination before branch-policy or close validation. GET /repos/unbraind/{repo}/pulls returns a same-repository numeric /repositories/{id}/pulls next-page Link that the old literal-path guard rejects. Real closeout jobs: pm-beads https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/40298977962/job/121491897462 ; pm-brief https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/40298856586/job/121491496493 ; pm-changelog https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40299074589/job/121492220507 ; pm-vcs https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40298876589/job/121491561782 . The fix verifies repository ID plus full_name before following the same-origin, same-endpoint alias.\n\nSync timestamp churn appears in pm-brief https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brief/actions/runs/40296846099/job/121484867381 and pm-vcs https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/40278487479/job/121426304352 . A real mixed new/native-linked batch reproduces on both 2026.10.19 and current 2026.10.26: an unmarked intermediate SDK UPDATE becomes external context and changes the transaction identity on repeat. The package skips an unnecessary item transaction only for a complete normalized matching projection with no unfinished GitHub journal; annotations, dependencies and privacy gates still run. Source/body formatting and assignment sentinels compare through the shared import normalizer; meaningful leading body indentation remains content.\n\npm-changelog https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40305700031/job/121514139043 correctly refuses absolute-host-path in bodies github-issue-226 and github-issue-1. That protection remains. Administration-only branch protection reads can also return HTTP 403 under GITHUB_TOKEN: the diagnostic now identifies the read and asks for required-checks, preserving readable ruleset/app bindings. SDK close refusals identify item, PR, validation code and missing fields. Both workflows select one privacy-checked annotation from private receipts.\n\nThe earlier complete npm gate passed 1540/1540 and exact 100/100/100/100 across 22 modules; it predates the final normalization adjustment. The full local Bun gate was stopped on the orchestrator instruction and is NOT a pass. No full local gate will be rerun. Current focused checks and CI own final verification; after push the CI wait is capped at 30 minutes. Both items remain open; caller adoption and source remediation stay in pm-github-samq. Main and latest release are still 2b71f73 and v2026.10.26; that release fixes neither incident trigger."
  "2026-10-27T09:45:59.719Z",codex-agent,"Final focused verification after the normalization adjustment: npm run build and npm run build:test passed. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/scheduled-refusals.test.ts test/import-regex.test.ts test/gate-inputs.test.ts passed 44/44, zero skipped/cancelled. node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"local edits invalidate|clean flow: gated import\" test/import-fidelity.test.ts test/import-gate.test.ts passed 2/2, including real interrupted-journal recovery and clean gated repeat import. npm run lint and npm run docstring passed. A first focused attempt caught the legacy string-tag representation; the final SDK parseTags implementation accepts it and preserves canonical comparison.\n\nAdditional behavioral revert proof: restoring ONLY normalizeImportValue() from origin/main makes node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"unchanged import comparison\" test/scheduled-refusals.test.ts fail 1/1; the final function was restored. The stronger real mixed-batch fixture now includes SDK-normalized body padding. Earlier recorded proofs remain: pages() revert fails --test-name-pattern=\"scheduled numeric pagination none\" test/scheduled-refusals.test.ts; runImport() revert fails --test-name-pattern=\"scheduled repeat\" test/scheduled-refusals.test.ts; closeoutFailureReason() revert fails --test-name-pattern=\"one workflow diagnostic identifies\" test/scheduled-refusals.test.ts; request error-stanza revert fails --test-name-pattern=\"non-retryable 404\" test/http-boundary.test.ts. Each proof uses node --test --test-concurrency=2, expects one failure, and restores the implementation before verification.\n\nNo full local gate was rerun after the resumed instruction. The prior npm 1540/1540 and exact four-dimensional coverage receipt predates the final normalizer. Full Bun was interrupted, not passed. Final full release gates belong to CI. Preparing the unmerged PR; the CI wait is capped at 30 minutes after push. Caller repositories remain untouched."
